ue that is actually attained within the set"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d5c439ff4397723d93bf34c7"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_minimum_of_a_set_c880c45a_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\min\\{1,2,3\\}$?","options":["$1$","$2$","$3$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1c8715a4fb7a966896a16159"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_minimum_of_a_set_c880c45a_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which set has minimum $0$?","options":["$(0,1)$","$[0,1)$","$(0,1]$","$\\{1,2,3\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ac05eac575a7c870641fa961"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_minimum_of_a_set_c880c45a_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why can a set have at most one minimum?","options":["A set cannot contain two real numbers","Every lower bound is automatically a minimum.","Two smallest elements must be $\\le$ each other, hence equal","The minimum is chosen arbitrarily"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"96e286909c66d1a7175ba09a"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_minimum_of_a_set_c880c45a_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How is the minimum related to the greatest lower bound when the minimum exists?","options":["The minimum is always larger than the greatest lower bound","The minimum is always the greatest lower bound of the set","The greatest lower bound cannot belong to the set","The minimum exists only when there are no lower bounds"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"249b1ba20bef56e1560c3271"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_minimum_of_a_set_c880c45a_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $E = \\{-2,0,3\\}$. Which statement is correct?","options":["$\\min E = 0$","$\\min E = 3$","$E$ has no minimum","$\\min E = -2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8dad108e4560f25f5dd744e7"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_mini